From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] leds: trigger: netdev: keep speed controls for SFP ports

An empty SFP cage may report only the MAC's initial interface modes.
Userspace then skips LED link-speed rules whose sysfs attributes are
hidden. Inserting a module exposes those attributes but never restores
the skipped rules, leaving a working 1G/2.5G link LED dark.

Keep the existing link-speed controls available for netdevices attached
to an SFP bus so LED rules can be armed before a module is inserted.
Retain supported-mode filtering for ports without an SFP bus and keep
the existing trigger and sysfs update locking.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
@@ -539,19 +539,26 @@
 	 * Stop at the first matching entry as we care only to check if a particular
 	 * speed is supported and not the kind.
 	 */
-	scoped_guard(mutex, &trigger_data->lock)
-		for_each_set_bit(mode, supported_link_modes, __ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_MASK_NBITS) {
-			struct ethtool_link_ksettings link_ksettings;
+	guard(mutex)(&trigger_data->lock);
 
-			ethtool_params_from_link_mode(&link_ksettings, mode);
+	/* SFP link modes change with the module. Keep speed controls writable
+	 * while the cage is empty so userspace can arm rules for later modules.
+	 */
+	if (trigger_data->net_dev && READ_ONCE(trigger_data->net_dev->sfp_bus))
+		return attr->mode;
+
+	for_each_set_bit(mode, supported_link_modes, __ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_MASK_NBITS) {
+		struct ethtool_link_ksettings link_ksettings;
+
+		ethtool_params_from_link_mode(&link_ksettings, mode);
 
-			CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(10);
-			CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(100);
-			CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(1000);
-			CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(2500);
-			CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(5000);
-			CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(10000);
-		}
+		CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(10);
+		CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(100);
+		CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(1000);
+		CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(2500);
+		CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(5000);
+		CHECK_LINK_MODE_ATTR(10000);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
